comment.narrative:
Survey of beneficiaries using&nbsp;Lot1 footbridges indicated an average reduction&nbsp;of travel time by 60% from the baseline 5 hours. M&amp;E work for completed Lot2 footbridges indicated that 64% of trips took less than 3 hours to get to schools and agricultural&nbsp;markets. While Lot3 M&amp;E indicated 88% of trips took less than 3 hour to markets and basic&nbsp;services, with 62 % of trips taking less than an hour.&nbsp;School travel time reduction has been the most&nbsp;significant with 49% of students at Raliee-Tuke and 54% at Mosamo taking less than 30 minutes to get to school- this, against the&nbsp;baseline travel time of 5 hours.





